    {
      "id": "N_FLAME_LINE_CAMP",
      "name": "The Fire-Line Camp",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 480,
      "cat": "Standard POI",
      "tier": 3,
      "factionId": "fac_pilgrim_party",
      "faction": "fac_pilgrim_party",
      "culture": "Clan",
      "customNotes": "**Sights:** Heat thickens at 40 li west of the village; the road is hot underfoot. **Events:** The pilgrims rest here after the failed fan test, twenty li back from the flames. The local spirit arrives with a hawk-beaked, fish-jawed demon carrying a copper pan of steamed cakes, puddings and yellow millet. **Tension:** Sha Monk's line 'where there are scriptures there is fire' is spoken here.",
